  "text": "Doctors | Cornell University Veterinary Specialists | Stamford, CT\nSkip to main content\nSearch:\nGo\nSearch Filters:\nThis Site\nCornell\nMenu\nSearch Cornell\n24-Hour Emergency\n(203) 595-2777\nPartner Portal\nAppointments\nPay Online\nDirections\nHome\nMain navigation\nAbout Us\nMission & Values\nOur People\nFAQ\nCareer Opportunities\nServices\nAnesthesiology\nDentistry, Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery\nDiagnostic Imaging\nEmergency & Critical Care\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology & Endoscopy\nOncology\nOphthalmology\nSurgery\nVeterinary Social Work\nLifeline Blood Bank\nSports Medicine & Rehabilitation\nDoctors\nSpecialty\nBentley, Adrienne\nBuriko, Kate\nDreese, Kaitlyn\nEmbriano, Kreig\nForman, Marnin\nGeddes, Alexander\nGonzalez, Anthony\nHackner, Susan\nLee, Bonnie\nLenfest, Margret\nLove, Edwina\nLyons, Bridget\nMazzaferro, Elisa\nMorgan, Oliver\nRoinestad, Karina\nSeller, Stephanie\nStanley, Emma\nWilson, Kendall\nWynne, Rachel Matusow\nZumbo, Brittany\nResidents\nClarke, Zenobya\nDamone, James\nHilfiker, Hailey\nKang, Aileen\nMercado Hernandez, Betzabeth\nPalleti, Neesha\nEmergency\nAndres, Katharine\nDeCillis, Rebecca\nGeisler, Laura\nReznicek, Eryn\nRigoli, Lindsay\nRoche, Michele\nFor Pet Owners\nPatient Registration\nFAQ for Pet Owners\nClient Experience\nOnline Payment Options\nResources\nSuccess Stories\nFor Veterinarians\nPartner Portal\nContinuing Education\nClinical Briefs\nCase Files\nArticles\nRequest Materials\nEducation\nPet Owners\nStudent Externships\nTechnicians\nVeterinarians\nAnnual CE Conference\nClinical Trials\nCanine Studies\nFeline Studies\nGiving\n24-Hour Emergency\n(203) 595-2777\nContact\nDoctors\nIn This Section:\nDoctors\nSpecialty\nBentley, Adrienne\nBuriko, Kate\nDreese, Kaitlyn\nEmbriano, Kreig\nForman, Marnin\nGeddes, Alexander\nGonzalez, Anthony\nHackner, Susan\nLee, Bonnie\nLenfest, Margret\nLove, Edwina\nLyons, Bridget\nMazzaferro, Elisa\nMorgan, Oliver\nRoinestad, Karina\nSeller, Stephanie\nStanley, Emma\nWilson, Kendall\nWynne, Rachel Matusow\nZumbo, Brittany\nResidents\nClarke, Zenobya\nDamone, James\nHilfiker, Hailey\nKang, Aileen\nMercado Hernandez, Betzabeth\nPalleti, Neesha\nEmergency\nAndres, Katharine\nDeCillis, Rebecca\nGeisler, Laura\nReznicek, Eryn\nRigoli, Lindsay\nRoche, Michele\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nDoctors\nWhen it comes to the people on the CUVS team, we set the bar pretty high. It’s an essential part of our mission to deliver unparalleled care\nand\nexceptional service.\nAt CUVS your pet is cared for by some of the top board-certified specialists in the nation, as well as a team of experienced, internship-trained emergency veterinarians. Our clinicians combine cutting-edge knowledge and expertise with a compassionate and collaborative, patient-centered approach.\nTo become a specialist takes real commitment. To become a specialist at CUVS takes even more. To specialize, veterinarians must undergo extensive post-doctorate training including, at minimum, a one-year internship, three years of intensive residency training in their chosen field, demonstration of meaningful contributions to veterinary science, publication of research findings in scientific journals, and completion of a rigorous, multi-day specialty board exam. Then these veterinarians achieve designation as diplomates of their respective specialty college.\nWhile other practices hire, we select\n- only those veterinarians whose clinical acumen, dedication and philosophy of care matches our culture.\nLearn more about the specialists and emergency veterinarians on the CUVS team:\nAnesthesiology\nElizabeth Goudie-DeAngelis\n, DVM, DACVAA\nDentistry and Oral Surgery\nAlexander Geddes\n, BVetMed, PGDip (VCP), DAVDC, MRCVS\nBonnie Lee\n, DVM, DAVDC\nDiagnostic Imaging\nS\ntephanie Seller\n, DVM, DACVR\nAlison Tarbell\n, DVM, DACVR\nKreig Embriano\n, VMD, MS, DACVR\nEmergency & Critical Care\nSusan G. Hackner\n, BVSc, MRCVS, DACVIM (SAIM), DACVECC\nBridget Lyons\n, VMD, DACVECC\nElisa Mazzaferro\n, MS, DVM, PhD, DACVECC\nAnthony Gonzalez\n, DVM, DACVECC\nKate Buriko\n, DVM, DACVECC\nKarina Roinestad\n, DVM, DACVECC\nKatharine Andres\n, DVM\nZenobya Clarke\n, DVM\nJames Damone\n, DVM\nRebecca DeCillis\n, DVM\nLaura Geisler\n, VMD\nHailey Hilfiker\n, DVM\nAileen Kang\n, DVM\nCat Neve\n, DVM\nEryn Reznicek\n, DVM\nLindsay Rigoli\n, DVM\nMichele Roche\n, DVM\nInternal Medicine\nMarnin Forman\n, DVM, DACVIM (SAIM)\nEmma Stanley\n, VMD, DACVIM (SAIM)\nKendall Wilson\n, DVM, DACVIM, (SAIM)\nInterventional Radiology & Endoscopy\nOliver Morgan\n, VMD, DACVS\nAdrienne Bentley\n, DVM, DACVS\nMarnin Forman\n, DVM, DACVIM (SAIM)\nOncology\nEdwina Love\n, DVM,\nDACVIM (Oncology)\nBrittnay Zumbo\n, DVM,\nDACVIM (Oncology)\nOphthalmology\nRachel Wynne\n, DVM, MS, DACVO\nSports Medicine & Rehabilitation\nDr. Margaret Lenfest\n, VMD, DACVSMR\nSurgery\nAdrienne Bentley,\nDVM, DACVS\nOliver Morgan\n, VMD, DACVS\nShare this:\nCUVS has 4 critical care specialists and 24/7 state-of-the-art care.\nAbout us\nmap\n880 Canal St, Stamford, CT 06902\nphone\n(203) 595-2777\nfax\n(203) 595-2778\nemail\ninfo@cuvs.org\nFollow us on:\nCornell University College of Veterinary Medicine\nCareer Opportunities\nUp\nBack to top",
